# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values, then restart `npm run dev`.
# The real `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Both values are the SAME ones already set in Netlify (Site configuration →
# Environment variables). They are not secrets in the usual sense: every VITE_
# variable is inlined into the browser bundle, so these already ship publicly on
# app.hotelthegrandalayna.com. Row-level security in Supabase is what protects
# the data, not the key.
#
# With these present, `npm run dev` loads the real hotel data locally. The dev
# session (see src/lib/devSession.js) skips the staff sign-in AND blocks every
# cloud write, so a local dev server can read the live data but cannot change it.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
